  <h3>Tiny Investments</h3>
  <p>I’m in the lucky position, after a successful exit, to be able to invest in people and things I genuinely believe in.</p>
  <p>I definitely have a bias for genuinely useful, premium quality stuff. I'm all in for long term value.</p>

  <h4>What I like to be involved in</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>B2B SaaS</strong>: Tangible products that make real business processes better. Think workflow tools, data products, and “boring but important” software with clear ROI.</li>
    <li><strong>D2C brands</strong>: Brands with a strong, authentic DNA focused on outdoors, sports, and wellbeing. Products people actually use and love in their day-to-day lives.</li>
    <li><strong>Tech-enabled services</strong>: Tech, sports, healthcare… As long as the focus is on quality, with a tech layer that makes the service smoother, smarter, and more scalable.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>How I like to help</h4>
  <p>I enjoy being hands-on where it matters and where it's welcomed.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Digital-first operations</strong> – setting up efficient, scalable processes from day one.</li>
    <li><strong>Tools for better customer experience</strong> - never at the expense of authenticity.</li>
    <li><strong>Growth &amp; go-to-market</strong> – pragmatic support on positioning, funnels, and retention.</li>
    <li><strong>Capital</strong> – backing founders with flexible, founder-friendly capital.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you’re building something in these spaces and this resonates, I’d love to hear from you.</p>
</BaseLayout>
